      "relationship_type": "5",
      "raw_relationship_type": "5",
      "rationale": "Control Discussion includes, \"Procedures can be documented in system security and privacy plans or in one or more separate documents.\"\r\n\r\nR1. mapping has a moderate relationship - SOR 5, but\r\nR1.2.3 and 1.2.6. mapping have a weak relationship - SOR 2",
      "source_locator": "Relationships-AC#row-6"
    },
    {
      "focal_id": "AC-02",
      "reference_id": "CIP-004-7",
      "relationship_type": "8",
      "raw_relationship_type": "8",
      "rationale": "R3.5 mapping is a moderate relationship - SOR 5\r\n\r\nR4/R5/R6 mapping has a strong relationship - SOR 8",
      "source_locator": "Relationships-AC#row-7"
    },
    {
      "focal_id": "AC-02",
      "reference_id": "CIP-007-6",
      "relationship_type": "5",
      "raw_relationship_type": "5",
      "rationale": "Mapping has a moderate relationship - SOR 5\r\n\r\nR5.2, R5.3 mapping have a strong relationship - SOR 8",
      "source_locator": "Relationships-AC#row-8"
    },
    {
      "focal_id": "AC-02(01)",
      "reference_id": "No Mapping",
      "relationship_type": "Concept Crosswalk",
      "raw_relationship_type": "Concept Crosswalk",
      "rationale": "CIP does not require automated mechanisms to manage system accounts; however, it does require documented processes for access management in CIP-004-7:\r\nR4. Implement documented access management programs\r\nR6. Implement documented access management programs to authorize, verify, and revoke provisioned access to BCSI\r\nCIP-007-6:\r\nR5.2. Identify and inventory all known enabled default or other generic account types, either by system, by groups of systems, by location, or by system types\r\nR5.3. Identify individuals who have authorized access to shared accounts\r\n\r\nModerate relationship - SOR 5",
      "source_locator": "Relationships-AC#row-9"
    },
    {
      "focal_id": "AC-02(02)",
      "reference_id": "No Mapping",
      "relationship_type": "Concept Crosswalk",
      "raw_relationship_type": "Concept Crosswalk",
      "rationale": "CIP does not require automatic removal or disabling temporary or emergency accounts after defined time period; however, it does require documented processes for access revocation: \r\nCIP-004-7\r\nR5. Implement documented access revocation programs\r\nR6.3. For termination actions, remove the individual’s ability to use provisioned access to information (BCSI) \r\n\r\nMapping has a weak relationship - SOR 2",
      "source_locator": "Relationships-AC#row-10"
    },
    {
      "focal_id": "AC-02(03)",
      "reference_id": "CIP-004-7",
      "relationship_type": "8",
      "raw_relationship_type": "8",
      "rationale": null,
      "source_locator": "Relationships-AC#row-11"
    },
    {
      "focal_id": "AC-02(04)",
      "reference_id": "No Mapping",
      "relationship_type": "Concept Crosswalk",
      "raw_relationship_type": "Concept Crosswalk",
      "rationale": "CIP does not require automatic audit of account creation, modification, enabling, disabling, and removal actions",
      "source_locator": "Relationships-AC#row-12"
    },
    {
